MDL502, F10: a misspelled masking function ("radnom_string") matches no known
function prefix; mydumper logs "Function not found: Using default" (only at
--verbose 3) and uses its identity function. Up to v0.21.2-4 that function
returns the value: users.email is dumped in plaintext. From v0.21.3-1 it
writes nothing into the output buffer: the column is dumped EMPTY. Exit 0
either way.
-- scenario --
tool: mydumper
versions: >= v0.19.1-1
args: --defaults-file /work/mydumper.cnf --host mysql --user e2e --password e2e-password --database app --verbose 3
lint: MDL502
expect config-loaded: true
expect exit: 0
expect stderr-contains: Function not found: Using default

when < v0.21.3-1
expect column app.users.email: plaintext
end

when >= v0.21.3-1
expect column app.users.email: empty
end
when kb:table-sections-ignored
# F17: this mydumper loses every table section (MDL511).
lint: MDL502, MDL511
end
-- mydumper.cnf --
[mydumper]
threads=2

[`app`.`users`]
`email`=radnom_string
